AB  - Higher education institutions increasingly regard alumni networks as important strategic assets. However, traditional alumni management systems generally suffer from fundamental flaws such as outdated data updates, broken communication channels, and a vacuum in value provision, which severely restrict alumni participation and weaken the emotional bond between universities and alumni. To address this challenge, this paper proposes and designs a new generation of alumni ecosystem deeply empowered by Artificial Intelligence (AI), positioning it as a core service component under the "Smart Campus"paradigm. The goal is to transform traditional alumni portals from static data warehouses into dynamic, service-centric value ecosystems. The system is built using a modern technology stack (Spring Boot 3, Vue 3, uni-app) and deeply integrates the DeepSeek Large Language Model (LLM) as the core intelligent engine. This paper focuses on elaborating the system's innovative architectural design, key technology selection reasons, and detailed introducing its core functions as a community and resource hub (such as same-city alumni connection, online and offline event organization, and alumni-exclusive career resource sharing). Research shows that by integrating powerful LLM with a robust enterprise-level Web architecture, a new generation of alumni platforms can be constructed to solve the pain points of traditional systems, with high practicality and forward-looking features. It provides an innovative architectural blueprint for improving alumni participation and contributes a key component to the vision of integrated, data-driven smart campuses. © 2025 IEEE.
