AB  - This paper presents a comprehensive evaluation of modern data architectures including Data Warehouse (DWH), Data Lake (DL), and Data Lakehouse (DLH) with a focus on their applicability in data-driven enterprises. The study identifies a robust set of criteria derived from both literature and practice to guide architecture selection. Using a weighted scoring methodology, each architecture is assessed based on its technical, organizational, and economic fit. The results indicate that DLH offers the best trade-off between scalability, flexibility, and support for advanced analytics, while traditional DWH solutions still excel in ease of use and implementation simplicity. The findings provide practical guidance for organizations navigating digital transformation and aiming to align data infrastructure with strategic goals. © 2025 The Author(s).
